          "title": "fix(run): read Forgejo's job list and run URLs",
          "body": "Fixes https://gitea.com/gitea/cli/issues/91\n\nOn Forgejo, `gt run view`, `gt run jobs` and `gt run logs` failed with \"invalid JSON response\", and a run URL from `gt pr checks` resolved to the wrong run.\n\n- Forgejo lists the jobs of a run in a bare array of its own shape. When the listing does not decode as Gitea's, gt reads it that way.\n- Forgejo's web URLs hold the position of the run in the repository and of the job in the run, not their IDs. A run or job URL is now matched against the `html_url` of the runs and jobs, so it selects the right one on both servers. This costs one extra request per run URL.\n\nThe version message that calls Forgejo \"Gitea 17.0.1\" is not changed here.\n",
